I like the rainbows that come after a storm. They are the best kind. The sky is still a bit grey, but then the sun peeps through the raindrops.

My favourite rainbow is a double one. You see a big, bright arch of colours. Red, orange, yellow, green, blue, indigo, violet. Then, just above it, there is a fainter, paler copy. It is like a shy ghost of the first one.

The colours are in the wrong order on the top one. It is a secret mirror in the sky. I think it looks like a magic bridge. It joins the wet, dark clouds to the happy, blue sky. It makes me feel safe and full of hope. [end of text]


